<%# Raise a change request (module 7 part 7.6; PRD §4.4 step 1).
    "Project/Cost Controller initiates BCR (what, why, $/period impact, schedule impact)."

    Two halves, and they are both required when money moves: the new BUDGET months, and the
    RESOURCE PLAN that supports them. Part 7.5 enforces "Σ buckets = the account's resource
    plan" in one transaction, so a change that adjusts only the money can never be approved.
    Asking for both here is what makes that approval possible rather than a surprise refusal
    days later.

    Title and sub-title come from `page()` in routes/bcr.js. %>
<% if (typeof error !== 'undefined' && error) { %>
<div class="errb"><div class="errb-tx"><p><b>Not recorded.</b> <%= error %></p></div></div>
<% } %>

<div class="note">
  <svg><use href="#i-info"/></svg>
  <span>Recording this <b>changes nothing</b>. It is a proposal: Finance verifies it, then the
    Project Manager approves it, and only then does the baseline move — from the effective month
    <b>forward</b>. The old figures are archived, not overwritten, and months already reported are
    never rewritten.</span>
</div>

<form method="post" action="/bcr">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">

  <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="card-hd"><h2>What is changing</h2>
      <span class="r">what, why, and how much</span></div>
    <div class="fbody">
      <div class="fgrid">
        <label class="fld">Kind of change
          <select name="change_type" required>
            <% types.forEach(function(t){ %>
            <option value="<%= t.code %>"><%= t.label %></option>
            <% }); %>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="fld">Work line
          <select name="wbs_node_id">
            <option value="">— not applicable (budget only) —</option>
            <% lines.forEach(function(l){ %>
            <option value="<%= l.id %>"><%= l.wbs_code %> · <%= l.name %></option>
            <% }); %>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="fld">Effective from (month)
          <input type="month" name="effective_period" required>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="fgrid">
        <label class="fld">Title
          <input type="text" name="title" maxlength="160" required
                 placeholder="e.g. Client asked for an extra 400 m2 of cladding">
        </label>
        <label class="fld">Cost impact (IDR)
          <input type="number" name="impact_cost" step="1" placeholder="0">
        </label>
        <label class="fld">Schedule impact (days)
          <input type="number" name="impact_schedule_days" step="1" placeholder="0">
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="fgrid">
        <label class="fld">Description
          <input type="text" name="description" maxlength="2000"
                 placeholder="what the change physically is">
        </label>
      </div>
      <label class="fld">Reason
        <input type="text" name="reason" maxlength="1000" required
               placeholder="why it is needed — this is what explains the movement later">
      </label>
      <p class="dim">A cost impact other than zero <b>must</b> come with the resource plan below.
        If the change only re-phases work without moving money, leave the impact at 0.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="card-hd"><h2>Resource plan the change carries</h2>
      <span class="r">rate × quantity, per work line and resource</span></div>
    <div class="fbody">
      <div class="note">
        <svg><use href="#i-info"/></svg>
        <span>The budget and the resource plan are required to agree, because the budget is the
          resource plan spread over months. Give the rows <b>after</b> the change: a new rate, new
          quantities, or a zero to retire a resource from the line. These are stored on the request
          and applied untouched at approval, so nobody edits them in between.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tw"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Work line</th><th>Resource</th><th>Cost account</th>
          <th class="r">Rate</th><th class="r">Qty</th><th>Unit</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% [0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7].forEach(function(i){ %>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <select name="r_node">
                <option value="">—</option>
                <% lines.forEach(function(l){ %>
                <option value="<%= l.id %>"><%= l.wbs_code %></option>
                <% }); %>
              </select>
            </td>
            <td>
              <select name="r_rbs_code">
                <option value="">—</option>
                <% resources.forEach(function(r){ %>
                <option value="<%= r.code %>"><%= r.code %> · <%= r.name %></option>
                <% }); %>
              </select>
            </td>
            <td>
              <select name="r_account">
                <option value="">— none —</option>
                <% accounts.forEach(function(a){ %>
                <option value="<%= a.id %>"><%= a.code %></option>
                <% }); %>
              </select>
            </td>
            <td class="r"><input type="number" name="r_rate" min="0" step="1" placeholder="0"></td>
            <td class="r"><input type="number" name="r_units" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="0"></td>
            <td><input type="text" name="r_unit_label" maxlength="24" placeholder="day"></td>
          </tr>
          <% }); %>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p class="dim">Leave a row blank to skip it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="card-hd"><h2>New budget months</h2>
      <span class="r">the proposed baseline, from the effective month forward</span></div>
    <div class="fbody">
      <div class="note">
        <svg><use href="#i-info"/></svg>
        <span>Enter the months this change sets, starting at or after the effective month. Each must
          name the work line it belongs to. At approval these replace the current figures from that
          month forward — everything before it is left exactly as reported.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tw"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>Work line</th><th>Cost account</th>
          <th class="r">Amount (IDR)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% [0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7].forEach(function(i){ %>
          <tr>
            <td><input type="month" name="month"></td>
            <td>
              <select name="node">
                <option value="">—</option>
                <% lines.forEach(function(l){ %>
                <option value="<%= l.id %>"><%= l.wbs_code %></option>
                <% }); %>
              </select>
            </td>
            <td>
              <select name="account">
                <option value="">—</option>
                <% accounts.forEach(function(a){ %>
                <option value="<%= a.id %>"><%= a.code %> · <%= a.name %></option>
                <% }); %>
              </select>
            </td>
            <td class="r"><input type="number" name="amount" min="0" step="1" placeholder="0"></td>
          </tr>
          <% }); %>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="fend" style="margin-top:12px">
    <a class="btn" href="/bcr">Cancel</a>
    <button class="btn pri" type="submit">Record the request</button>
  </div>
</form>

<svg style="display:none" aria-hidden="true"><defs>
<symbol id="i-info" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12 3a9 9 0 1 0 0 18 9 9 0 0 0 0-18Zm-2.6 2.4h1.2v12.1H9.5z"/></symbol>
</defs></svg>
